WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.300
Objection: "Nice idea, but it likely won't happen.". Response: It already did.

2
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:10.160
The Oxford RECOVERY trial tested seven treatments in six months, saved one million lives at five hundred dollars per patient.

3
00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:16.520
The F.D.A.'s version costs forty-one thousand dollars per patient for the same information.

4
00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:23.360
The trial used existing hospital systems. Hospitals, it turns out, already contain sick people.

5
00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:27.860
This was apparently news. Follow-up: "But globally?". Response: The internet scaled globally.

6
00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:32.640
So did smartphones. So did TikTok, which is considerably less useful.

7
00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:44.040
This just scales what already worked. We Need the Military Budget Objection: "We can't reduce military spending.

8
00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:44.040
That would make us vulnerable.". Response: The treaty takes one percent.

9
00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:47.560
You keep ninety-nine percent. If you can't defend yourself with ninety-nine percent of history's largest military budget,

10
00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:56.080
the problem isn't money. The Pentagon literally cannot account for two point five trillion dollars in spending.

11
00:00:56.580 --> 00:01:00.240
You're asking them to redirect money they already lost in the couch cushions.

12
00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:07.780
Every nation reduces by one percent, so relative military balance stays proportional.

13
00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:13.500
Everyone turns the volume down together. Nobody gets quieter relative to anyone else.

14
00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:18.100
The greatest threats today aren't tanks rolling over borders.

15
00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:23.040
They're microscopic things rolling through airports. C.O.V.I.D.

16
00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:31.880
nineteen killed more Americans than World War One, World War Two, Korea, Vietnam, Iraq, and Afghanistan combined.

17
00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:41.180
It did this without triggering a single defense system. Your nine hundred ninety-nine billion dollar military budget watched

18
00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:47.640
it happen, fully armed and completely useless. Broke, sick countries start wars.

19
00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:55.200
Healthy countries start businesses. Curing disease is preventative defense with better R.O.I.

20
00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:58.560
than any missile system ever built. Follow-up: "But what if enemies don't reduce?".

21
00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:06.460
Response: That's what a treaty is. Everyone signs at once. Those who don't simply miss Incentive Alignment Bond benefits.

22
00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:10.960
Their politicians lose campaign funding and post-office opportunities.

23
00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:17.480
Participating nations' politicians get rewarded instead. Self-interest does the heavy lifting.

24
00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:22.460
It always does. Big Pharma Will Block This Objection: "Pharmaceutical companies will kill this.

25
00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:27.900
They profit from disease.". Response: Pharma makes MORE money under this model.

26
00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:31.140
Watch their opposition evaporate. Current system: Pharma pays two point six zero billion dollars per drug.

27
00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:40.580
Ninety percent fail. Only blockbusters profit. The business model is "spend billions gambling, hope one pill pays for the

28
00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:46.860
nine that didn't work.". New system: The treaty fund pays pharma to run trials.

29
00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:53.480
Trials become revenue, not cost. More drugs become profitable, even the weird ones.

30
00:02:54.280 --> 00:03:02.000
Predictable income instead of pharmaceutical roulette. Pharma would lobby FOR this harder than they've ever lobbied for

31
00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:07.600
anything. You'd be giving drug companies more money to do what they already do.

32
00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:13.540
They'd trample each other getting to the signing ceremony. What About National Sovereignty?

33
00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:16.560
Objection: "This forces countries to spend money a certain way.

34
00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:19.580
That violates sovereignty." Response: No force involved. Countries sign by choice.

35
00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:21.060
Don't want to? Don't. Miss out on the benefits. Citizens demand it?

36
00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:27.780
Sign. This is how democracy is supposed to work. I understand you may be unfamiliar with the concept.

37
00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:31.500
Follow-up: "What if our government doesn't want to?". Response: Vote them out.

38
00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:34.100
This is also how democracy works. (I'm told you've done this before.).

39
00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:38.560
"The F.D.A. Exists for a Reason" Objection: "We need F.D.A.

40
00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:48.440
approval to ensure safety. You're being reckless." Response: The F.D.A.

41
00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:49.160
is a lifeguard who won't throw the life preserver until it passes a twelve-year safety review.

42
00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:49.160
By which point you have drowned, decomposed, and become a coral reef.

43
00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:55.940
F.D.A. delays from nineteen sixty-two to the present have caused four to ten million American deaths from drug lag.

44
00:03:56.820 --> 00:04:02.440
F.D.A. prevented disasters include maybe thalidomide, which caused one thousand deaths.

45
00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:11.640
The net result is that F.D.A. policies may have contributed to four thousand to ten thousand deaths for every life saved.

46
00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:18.200
Under the decentralized framework for drug assessment, patients see real data on risks and benefits.

47
00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:25.840
Then they decide. The radical concept of adults making informed choices about their own bodies.

48
00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:31.460
"What If Countries Cheat?" Objection: "Countries will promise to reduce military spending but won't."

49
00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:32.380
Response: The system doesn't rely on trust. (Good, because you have none.) It relies on incentives.

50
00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:41.080
Politicians who comply receive Incentive Alignment Bond benefits, including campaign funding and post-office career opportunities.

51
00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:48.940
Politicians who don't comply get nothing. Contributions are public on blockchain, so compliance is verifiable.

52
00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:53.500
Smart contracts route benefits automatically to compliant participants.

53
00:04:55.260 --> 00:05:01.540
Traditional treaties rely on trust and shame. This one makes compliance the career-maximizing choice.

54
00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:06.140
Politicians comply because it's profitable, not because they grew a conscience.

55
00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:11.580
(They didn't.). "You Can't Cure Aging" Objection: "Aging is natural and inevitable.

56
00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:13.060
You can't fight nature." Response: Dying from infected teeth was "natural" until dentistry.

57
00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:18.670
Dying in childbirth was "natural" until medicine. Dying of smallpox was "natural" until vaccines.

58
00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:28.080
"Natural" just means "nobody's fixed it yet." Dying of old age is "natural" in the same way dying of anything is natural.

59
00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:36.180
You're just used to this one. You already replace everything that breaks: Hearts are replaced (you're basically a car at

60
00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:40.520
this point). Kidneys are replaced (or we hook you to a machine thrice weekly).

61
00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:48.140
Blood is replaced (vampire economics, but medical). Bones are replaced (titanium is better anyway).

62
00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:51.940
Joints are replaced (your grandma is fifteen percent metal).

63
00:05:52.760 --> 00:06:01.080
Aging is damage accumulation with known repair pathways: Telomeres shorten: lengthen them (telomerase activation).

64
00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:09.420
Cells senesce: clear them (senolytic drugs). Proteins misfold: refold them (molecular chaperones).

65
00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:18.360
Mitochondria fail: replace them (mitochondrial transfer). DNA breaks: repair it (CRISPR, base editing).

66
00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:23.880
You went to the moon with slide rules. You can probably fix cells with A.I.

67
00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:31.220
Your body is a machine. Machines can be repaired. Aging is harder engineering, not magic.

68
00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:35.880
You keep confusing the two because it makes you feel better about not trying.

69
00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:43.180
"I'm Just One Person". Objection: "My vote/investment/share won't matter.

70
00:06:43.660 --> 00:06:48.970
I'm too small." Response: This needs two hundred eighty million people.

71
00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:55.080
You tell ten. They each tell ten. Six degrees of sharing reaches millions.

72
00:06:55.600 --> 00:07:01.390
It's a pyramid scheme, except at the end everyone lives longer instead of losing their savings.

73
00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:07.900
Your contribution: vote (two minutes), buy bonds (ten minutes), share (fifteen minutes).

74
00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:16.280
Total: twenty-seven minutes. Potential return: fifty thousand extra hours of life if diseases get cured.

75
00:07:16.940 --> 00:07:21.340
That's the best trade you'll ever make, and you've made some terrible ones.

76
00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:28.140
"Reform the System Instead". Objection: "Why not just reform the F.D.A.

77
00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:32.940
and N.I.H.?" Response: People have been trying for fifty years.

78
00:07:33.540 --> 00:07:37.460
Here's the scorecard: More funding? Tried. They bought more paperwork.

79
00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:43.820
Different leadership? Tried. Same results, fancier titles. New regulations?

80
00:07:44.280 --> 00:07:48.080
Tried. Now takes twenty years instead of seventeen. Progress.

81
00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:53.360
Reform bills? Tried. Lobbyists killed them in committee. Efficiently.

82
00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:58.780
You keep trying to teach a fish to climb a tree. The fish isn't broken.

83
00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:03.840
It's a fish. The system is hard to fix because it IS working.

84
00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:12.400
Just not for you. Defense contractors spend one hundred twenty-seven million dollars yearly on lobbying and get nearly one

85
00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:19.780
trillion dollars in contracts. That's not a broken system. That's the most efficient system in American capitalism.

86
00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:25.120
They won't surrender it because you asked nicely. Don't reform the system.

87
00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:33.039
Build around it. "This Is Politically Impossible". Objection: "No government will agree to this.

88
00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:38.860
Pure fantasy." Response: Politicians follow money the way rivers follow gravity.

89
00:08:39.679 --> 00:08:44.000
The aim: make this the easiest, most profitable decision of their careers.

90
00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:50.500
The military-industrial complex spends one hundred twenty-seven million dollars yearly on lobbyists.

91
00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:56.760
You can't beat them with moral arguments. (They're immune.) Beat them at their own game.

92
00:08:57.540 --> 00:09:03.900
Raise one billion dollars through VICTORY Bonds. Allocate six hundred fifty million dollars for lobbying.

93
00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:08.760
That overwhelms the defense industry's one hundred twenty-seven million dollar spend.

94
00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:15.650
Go to the same K-Street firms defense contractors use. Outbid them for their top talent.

95
00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:19.900
Lobbyists work for the highest bidder. Become the highest bidder.

96
00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:27.580
Politicians suddenly hear more about curing cancer and less about threats from countries they can't find on maps.

97
00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:36.920
This isn't fantasy. It's capitalism. Once two hundred eighty million voters demand it and the money is behind it, refusal

98
00:09:36.920 --> 00:09:42.820
becomes career suicide. Politicians are very good at not committing career suicide.

99
00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:50.340
What If the Science Is Wrong? Objection: "What if we fund one hundred thousand trials and nothing gets cured?".

100
00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:56.160
Response: Worst case: you learn, with high certainty, one hundred thousand things that don't work.

101
00:09:56.960 --> 00:10:04.180
Edison found ten thousand ways not to make a lightbulb. You'd find one hundred thousand ways not to cure cancer.

102
00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:08.580
That's called science. You've been doing it for four hundred years.

103
00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:13.780
It's the only method you have that actually works. Maybe use it more.

104
00:10:14.600 --> 00:10:20.970
Still better than the current system: One hundred trials over seventeen years, learn nothing, many retire wealthy.

105
00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:27.220
N.I.H. funding safe research confirming water is wet. F.D.A.

106
00:10:27.220 --> 00:10:32.180
blocking trials because the paperwork had a typo on page eight hundred forty-seven.

107
00:10:33.020 --> 00:10:39.060
The decentralized framework runs forty-four point one times more trials for the same budget.

108
00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:44.560
Even if ninety percent fail, you get ten times more cures than today.

109
00:10:45.400 --> 00:10:49.920
Failure at scale is still more productive than success at a standstill.

110
00:10:51.220 --> 00:11:00.820
I Don't Have Time Objection: "I'm too busy.". Response: Vote (two minutes), buy bonds (ten minutes), share (fifteen minutes).

111
00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:06.800
Total: twenty-seven minutes. You spent longer than that choosing what to watch on Netflix last night.

112
00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:15.220
If diseases get cured, you save hundreds of hours in doctor visits and sick days, plus potentially tens of thousands of

113
00:11:15.220 --> 00:11:21.560
hours of extra life. That's a one hundred eleven thousand percent return on twenty-seven minutes.

114
00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:27.700
This Is Unrealistic Objection: "This will never happen. You're naive about human nature.".

115
00:11:28.840 --> 00:11:36.800
Response: Your species has an impressive track record of calling things unrealistic, then doing them, then pretending you

116
00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:44.820
always knew they were possible. Things that were "unrealistic": Human flight (impossible for millennia, then two bicycle

117
00:11:44.820 --> 00:11:51.290
mechanics). Moon landing (J.F.K. did it in nine years with computers weaker than your toaster).

118
00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:56.720
Democracy (kings ruled for five thousand years, then didn't).

119
00:11:57.280 --> 00:12:05.680
Ending slavery (entire economies depended on it). Women voting (half the population was excluded, the other half thought

120
00:12:05.680 --> 00:12:10.820
this was fine). The internet (who needs computers talking to each other?).

121
00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:19.360
What's actually unrealistic: Spending two point seven two trillion dollars on weapons while sitting on thirteen thousand

122
00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:23.540
nuclear warheads. That's enough for one hundred thirty extinction events.

123
00:12:24.420 --> 00:12:29.260
You only need one. Expecting different results from the same broken system.

124
00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:33.880
Thinking you'll survive the A.I. revolution without fixing incentives.

125
00:12:35.080 --> 00:12:38.900
Fifty-five million people die each year from treatable causes.

126
00:12:39.580 --> 00:12:47.080
That's the unrealistic thing. You just got used to it. War Is Human Nature Objection: "War is inevitable.

127
00:12:47.580 --> 00:12:53.760
Countries need militaries to survive.". Response: Several countries beg to differ.

128
00:12:54.460 --> 00:13:02.500
Switzerland: Over two hundred years avoiding major wars. Surrounded by both World Wars (literally in the middle, made chocolate).

129
00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:08.540
G.D.P. per capita: ninety-three thousand dollars (not killing people is profitable).

130
00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:18.020
Defense spending: zero point seven percent of G.D.P. Life expectancy: eighty-four years (five years longer than Americans

131
00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:26.940
who spend five times more on "defense"). Costa Rica: Abolished its army in nineteen forty-eight (said "nah, we're good").

132
00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:32.920
Still sovereign seventy-five plus years later (nobody invaded the country with no oil).

133
00:13:33.840 --> 00:13:40.560
Redirected military budget to education and health. Life expectancy matches U.S.

134
00:13:40.560 --> 00:13:47.360
at a fraction of the cost. Zero invasions since (turns out nobody wants to conquer happy, educated people).

135
00:13:48.380 --> 00:13:52.800
The pattern is not subtle: countries choosing peace get richer.

136
00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:59.040
Countries choosing war get poorer. Countries drained by disease are unstable and start fights.

137
00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:05.160
Countries investing in their people become too prosperous and comfortable to bother picking them.

138
00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:12.000
Nuclear weapons made territorial conquest largely obsolete in nineteen forty-five.

139
00:14:12.060 --> 00:14:21.070
You're still budgeting like it's nineteen forty-four. All Wars on X Have Failed Objection: "War on Drugs, War on Poverty,

140
00:14:21.280 --> 00:14:28.580
War on Terror all failed. This will too." Response: Those were government wars using central planning.

141
00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:37.600
This uses markets. Spot the difference. Why government "wars" fail: They create bureaucracies that need the problem to exist.

142
00:14:38.280 --> 00:14:43.320
The War on Drugs needs drug crime. The War on Poverty needs poor people.

143
00:14:43.880 --> 00:14:51.920
The War on Terror needs enemies. Each one accidentally created a government department whose continued employment depends

144
00:14:51.920 --> 00:14:55.680
on the problem never being solved. It's impressive, really.

145
00:14:56.440 --> 00:15:03.640
The only war humanity won decisively was World War Two. And that was against other humans, which is admittedly your area

146
00:15:03.640 --> 00:15:09.280
of expertise. When you declare war on abstract concepts, the concepts win.

147
00:15:09.780 --> 00:15:14.140
Why the War on Disease is different: Uses markets, not ministries.

148
00:15:14.860 --> 00:15:19.940
Pays for outcomes, not process. No bureaucracy to preserve (smart contracts).

149
00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:25.680
Competition between solutions. Researchers paid for cures, not grants.

150
00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:30.640
You're not declaring war on disease. You're declaring peace with biology.

151
00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:35.100
Then letting markets optimize. Call it the Market for Health.

152
00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:42.400
It's less dramatic, but it might actually work. This Sounds Like Bribery Objection: "You're just bribing politicians.

153
00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:49.480
That's illegal and immoral." Response: Current "legal" lobbying is bribery with better stationery.

154
00:15:49.860 --> 00:15:58.140
It currently produces war, disease, and existential risk. This applies the same mechanics, transparently, to save lives

155
00:15:58.140 --> 00:16:03.440
instead. The status quo kills people. This kills fewer people.

156
00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:12.440
If you're confused about the ethics, count the bodies. It's Unenforceable Objection: "Government promises to pay are unenforceable

157
00:16:12.440 --> 00:16:19.060
fantasy." Response: Courts are slow. Money is fast. This doesn't rely on courts.

158
00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:22.720
Break your word, the system automatically funds your replacement.

159
00:16:23.600 --> 00:16:26.540
Politicians understand this incentive structure instinctively.

160
00:16:27.240 --> 00:16:33.840
It's the only language they're truly fluent in. You Can't Verify Two Hundred Eighty Million People Objection: "Impossible

161
00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:34.740
to verify two hundred eighty million people online without fraud."

162
00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:41.820
Response: You already verify hundreds of millions of people for banking, government services, insurance, and online gambling.

163
00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:46.720
You can verify people for the purpose of not dying. It's the same technology.

164
00:16:47.420 --> 00:16:52.740
The stakes are just higher and the forms are shorter. Government I.D.s use national e-I.D.

165
00:16:53.060 --> 00:17:00.160
systems (Estonia, India, E.U.). Biometrics like fingerprints and face scans ensure unique individuals.

166
00:17:00.880 --> 00:17:05.400
A.I. fraud detection uses algorithms to spot suspicious patterns.

167
00:17:05.700 --> 00:17:11.040
Math verification enables end-to-end verifiable voting with zero-knowledge proofs.

168
00:17:11.819 --> 00:17:17.000
This is a solved problem wearing an unsolved hat. Why Not Just Use Philanthropy?

169
00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:22.800
Objection: "If this matters, why not raise money from donors instead of complicated bonds?"

170
00:17:23.540 --> 00:17:29.060
Response: All philanthropy combined is a rounding error compared to government budgets.

171
00:17:29.700 --> 00:17:34.940
A massive campaign would cannibalize donations from health charities already doing critical work.

172
00:17:35.460 --> 00:17:42.060
You'd be stealing from cancer research to fund cancer research, which is impressively pointless even by your standards.

173
00:17:42.760 --> 00:17:50.720
The goal is tapping the multi-trillion dollar stream of wasted government spending, not reshuffling the charity tip jar.

174
00:17:51.220 --> 00:17:57.840
How Do You Prevent Waste? Objection: "How do you ensure money helps patients instead of funding bureaucracy?"

175
00:17:58.580 --> 00:18:07.720
Response: The decentralized framework for drug assessment, or D.F.D.A., model achieves eighty times lower cost per patient.

176
00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:13.560
Pragmatic trials cost five hundred dollars. Traditional trials cost forty-one thousand dollars.

177
00:18:14.180 --> 00:18:22.980
Same science. Eighty times less overhead. The N.I.H.'s RECOVER initiative spent one point six billion dollars over four

178
00:18:22.980 --> 00:18:31.940
years and completed zero trials. Zero. With that same budget, the decentralized model could have run thousands of trials

179
00:18:31.940 --> 00:18:37.920
for millions of patients. The N.I.H. managed to spend all that money learning nothing.

180
00:18:38.640 --> 00:18:45.480
That takes talent. Why Not Just Increase Health Funding? Objection: "Why cut military spending?

181
00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:51.480
Just allocate more money to health research." Response: Money isn't the only constraint.

182
00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:57.340
You can't print more physicists. (You've tried. It takes twenty-five years and a P.h.D.

183
00:18:57.520 --> 00:19:02.390
program.). Cutting one percent from military budgets doesn't just move dollars.

184
00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:07.380
It frees actual human brains from building weapons to curing Alzheimer's.

185
00:19:07.920 --> 00:19:11.160
Right now your smartest people are optimizing missile trajectories.

186
00:19:11.640 --> 00:19:15.840
Those same brains could optimize drug molecules. The brains don't care.

187
00:19:16.200 --> 00:19:19.840
They just go where the funding is. What About Defense Industry Jobs?

188
00:19:20.620 --> 00:19:25.080
Objection: "This will destroy millions of military industry jobs."

189
00:19:25.570 --> 00:19:32.300
Response: The U.S. contribution is less than zero point five percent of trillions of dollars the Pentagon can't account

190
00:19:32.300 --> 00:19:37.620
for. You're not destroying jobs. You're redirecting ghost money into real ones.

191
00:19:38.760 --> 00:19:42.860
Engineers building guidance systems can build medical imaging devices.

192
00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:50.260
Same skills, fewer explosions, more job satisfaction surveys where nobody ticks "my work kills people."

193
00:19:51.100 --> 00:19:56.220
This Violates Election Law Objection: "Foreign nationals funding U.S.

194
00:19:56.220 --> 00:19:59.280
elections is illegal, and your bonds sound like securities."

195
00:19:59.960 --> 00:20:03.760
Response: Hire good lawyers. Defense contractors figured this out decades ago.

196
00:20:04.380 --> 00:20:07.500
You can too. Separate legal entities in each country, zero coordination on political spending.

197
00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:12.340
